From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:13:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] libcamera: camera_sensor_properties: Add SuperPix SP2508

Exposure and analogue gain are latched together by the sensor update
register, so both take effect after the same number of frames. The
vendor 3A applies them in the same frame (AEShutDelayFrame and
AESensorGainDelayFrame are both 0, AEISPGainDelayFrame is 1). The unit
cell size is not documented.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
index e2f518f..3541bfd 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/sensor/camera_sensor_properties.cpp
@@ -456,6 +456,18 @@ const CameraSensorProperties *CameraSensorProperties::get(const std::string &sen
 			},
 			.sensorDelays = { },
 		} },
+		{ "sp2508", {
+			.testPatternModes = {
+				{ controls::draft::TestPatternModeOff, 0 },
+				{ controls::draft::TestPatternModeColorBars, 1 },
+			},
+			.sensorDelays = {
+				.exposureDelay = 2,
+				.gainDelay = 2,
+				.vblankDelay = 2,
+				.hblankDelay = 2
+			},
+		} },
 	};
 
 	const auto it = sensorProps.find(sensor);
